SELECT STORE_REF FROM INV_VOUCHER WHERE ID = 001;
OR 
SELECT STORE_REF2 FROM INV_VOUCHER WHERE ID = 001;

Please note that neither of these queries will necessarily return a "type" of store, they will only return the reference to another table which may contain more information. The type of store would not be directly available from this schema without additional tables or data.
Also, it's important to mention that ID = 001 might not work depending on how the database is set up to interpret numerical IDs. It could potentially need to be ID = 1 instead.

SELECT PART_REF, SL_TITLE FROM INV_VOUCHER_ITEM WHERE PART_REF = '8143000120';

OR

SELECT * FROM INV_PART WHERE ID = '8143000120';

(در صورتی که جدول INV_PART وجود داشته باشد و حاوی اطلاعات مربوط به کالاها باشد)

SELECT SUPPLIER_TITLE FROM INV_VOUCHER WHERE TITLE = 'VS_EXP_005'; 
OR 
SELECT SUPPLIER_TITLE, CONTRACTOR_TITLE FROM INV_VOUCHER_ITEM WHERE SL_TITLE = 'VS_EXP_005';
The exact SQL query depends on where the information is stored in your database schema. The provided schema does not specify whether VS_EXP_005 is an internal or external purchase pattern, nor does it indicate which table and field this information would be located in. Therefore, these queries are based on assumptions about where such data might be found. Please adjust according to the actual structure of your database.
The first query assumes that 'VS_EXP_005' is a title stored in the INV_VOUCHER table associated with supplier information. The second query assumes that 'VS_EXP_005' is an SL_TITLE stored in the INV_VOUCHER_ITEM table, also potentially related to supplier or contractor information.
Please replace 'VS_EXP_005' and field names as necessary based on your actual data structure.

SELECT COST_CENTER_TITLE 
FROM INV_VOUCHER 
WHERE ID = 540122301;

SELECT * FROM INV_VOUCHER WHERE DATE = CURDATE() AND STATE = 'بطل شده' AND STORE_REF = 'انبار مواد اولیه مصرفی'; 
Please note that "STORE_REF = 'انبار مواد اولیه مصرفی'" might not work if the store_ref is a reference to another table and does not directly contain the name of the warehouse. In this case, you would need to join with the relevant table(s) to filter on the warehouse name. Also CURDATE() function gives today's date in SQL.
However, based on provided schema we can't determine data type of STORE_REF field so this query might need adjustment.

SELECT SUPPLIER_TITLE 
FROM INV_VOUCHER 
WHERE DESCRIPTION LIKE '%لپ تاپ ASUS%' AND STATE = 'تایید شده' AND DATE = DATE_SUB(CURDATE(), INTERVAL 1 DAY);
